\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces C1 under identical perfect-channel training. Feature erasure uses the exact first expected-distance term. Centered lognormal output noise uses the closed-form Gaussian-reference expression in the second inequality. Risk-upper curves include empirical risk, its MC correction, and the data penalty. The lognormal direct-expectation MC curve is a diagnostic, not a certified risk upper; its distance estimates never enter the reference bound. The Jensen curve is a separate analytic upper bound. Held-out-risk error bars show one sample SD over all three seeds. Uncapped bounds above one are vacuous.}}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:sim_c1_evaluation}{{4}{5}{}{figure.4}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {III}{\ignorespaces Test performance, reused-bank empirical risk, and bounds. Training counts are $n=55{,}000$ for MNIST, $n=10{,}000$ for FashionMNIST, and $n=45{,}000$ for CIFAR-10; all use $m=100$. Perfect denotes training only. Accuracy is in percent; risks use $-\log (0.01+0.99p_y)/\log 100$. Test risk is a held-out estimate. Entries are mean $\pm $ sample SD over all selected seeds (three for MNIST/CIFAR-10, two for FashionMNIST), with ten Gibbs/channel draws. Unweighted T1/T2 bounds include fresh empirical Monte Carlo correction and total failure budget $0.05$: $0.04/(2\times 51)$ per theorem/run and $0.01/51$ per MC event. Values above one are vacuous; final clipping gives one. N/A denotes deterministic ERM/L2, whose Dirac posterior has infinite KL to the continuous Gaussian prior. Bounds concern smooth Gibbs loss under the theorem assumptions and declared confidence family.}}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:sim_algorithm_risk_bounds}{{III}{5}{}{table.3}{}}
\newlabel{tab:sim_accuracy_risk}{{III}{5}{}{table.3}{}}
\newlabel{tab:sim_cifar}{{III}{5}{}{table.3}{}}
