\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {X}{\ignorespaces C1 evaluation with identical perfect-channel training: the same three frozen posteriors face either hidden-feature erasures or centered lognormal output-logit noise. Test accuracy and risk are mean $\pm $ sample SD across all three seeds; risks use normalized smooth loss. Empirical risk, the data term, and the fresh empirical-MC correction are shared by both deployment cases. Erasure uses C1's first inequality with the discrete metric and $K=1$. Centered lognormal output noise uses the second inequality with the Euclidean metric and $K=\sqrt  2/\log 100$. For lognormal rows, the first term is an independent MC diagnostic (not a certified bound); the risk upper uses the analytic second term. The upper columns are uncapped means of the per-seed bounds, which include empirical MC error; values above one are vacuous.}}{9}{}\protected@file@percent }
